  /* ---------------- Verbal reasoning passages (True / False / Cannot say) ---------------- */
  B.verbal = [
    { p: 'Airline pilots in many countries must undergo simulator checks every six months. These checks include handling engine failures, rejected take-offs and emergency descents. A pilot who fails a check is usually given additional training before being re-tested.', s: [['Pilots who fail a simulator check are always removed from flying permanently.', 'F'], ['Simulator checks include rejected take-offs.', 'T'], ['Most pilots fail at least one simulator check in their career.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'Fog forms most often on clear, calm nights when the ground loses heat quickly. In northern India such fog is common in winter and can close airports for several hours after sunrise. Instrument landing systems allow suitably equipped aircraft and trained crews to land in lower visibility than would otherwise be possible.', s: [['Fog in northern India is most common in winter.', 'T'], ['All aircraft can land in fog if the airport has an instrument landing system.', 'F'], ['Fog is more dangerous than thunderstorms.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'The company introduced a fatigue-reporting system last year. Crew may file a fatigue report without penalty. Since its introduction the number of reports has risen sharply, which managers believe reflects greater trust rather than more fatigue.', s: [['Crew are penalised for filing fatigue reports.', 'F'], ['Managers believe the rise in reports shows greater trust.', 'T'], ['Fatigue among crew has actually decreased.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'A new regional airport opened with a single runway of 2,200 metres. It can handle narrow-body jets but not fully loaded wide-body aircraft. The state government has announced plans to extend the runway within five years.', s: [['The airport currently cannot handle fully loaded wide-body aircraft.', 'T'], ['The runway extension has already begun.', 'C'], ['The airport has two runways.', 'F']] },
    { p: 'Sustainable aviation fuel can be blended with conventional jet fuel and used in existing engines. It currently costs considerably more than conventional fuel. Producers say costs will fall as production increases.', s: [['Sustainable aviation fuel requires new engines.', 'F'], ['Sustainable aviation fuel is currently more expensive than conventional fuel.', 'T'], ['Sustainable aviation fuel will be cheaper than conventional fuel within five years.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'The training school accepts applicants aged 18 to 30 who hold a Class 1 medical certificate. Applicants must pass an aptitude test and an interview. Those who pass the aptitude test but fail the interview may reapply after six months.', s: [['A 31-year-old applicant is eligible.', 'F'], ['An applicant who fails the interview can reapply after six months.', 'T'], ['Most applicants fail the aptitude test.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'Bird strikes occur most often during take-off and landing, when aircraft are close to the ground where birds are most numerous. Airports use techniques such as habitat management and sound devices to discourage birds. No method has eliminated bird strikes entirely.', s: [['Bird strikes are most common at cruising altitude.', 'F'], ['Some airports use sound devices against birds.', 'T'], ['Habitat management is the most effective method.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'Every flight crew member must hold a valid licence, a valid medical certificate and current type rating. The operator checks these documents before rostering. In addition, crew must complete annual recurrent training on emergency equipment.', s: [['The operator checks documents before rostering.', 'T'], ['Emergency equipment training is required once every two years.', 'F'], ['Crew who forget their licence are fined.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'Turbulence is the leading cause of injuries to passengers and cabin crew on large aircraft. Most injured people were not wearing seat belts at the time. Airlines therefore advise passengers to keep belts fastened whenever seated.', s: [['Most people injured in turbulence were not wearing seat belts.', 'T'], ['Turbulence causes most aircraft accidents.', 'C'], ['Airlines advise passengers to unfasten belts when the sign is off.', 'F']] },
    { p: 'The cadet programme lasts about 24 months. The first phase is ground school; the second is flying training abroad; the final phase is type rating training. Cadets who do not meet the required standard in any phase may be removed from the programme.', s: [['Type rating training comes before ground school.', 'F'], ['Cadets can be removed for not meeting the standard.', 'T'], ['Flying training abroad lasts exactly 12 months.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'Low-cost carriers reduce costs by operating a single aircraft type, maximising aircraft utilisation and selling tickets directly. A single fleet type simplifies pilot training and spare parts.', s: [['Operating one aircraft type simplifies pilot training.', 'T'], ['Low-cost carriers sell tickets only through travel agents.', 'F'], ['Low-cost carriers are safer than full-service airlines.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'Cockpit voice recorders capture conversations and sounds on the flight deck. Investigators use them, together with flight data recorders, to understand the sequence of events in an accident. Recordings are protected and are not normally released to the public.', s: [['Cockpit voice recorders capture flight-deck conversations.', 'T'], ['Investigators use only the cockpit voice recorder.', 'F'], ['Recordings are usually published within a month.', 'F']] },
    { p: 'Monsoon rains reach Kerala around the beginning of June and usually cover the whole country by mid-July. The timing varies from year to year. A delayed onset can affect agriculture and water supply.', s: [['The monsoon always reaches Kerala on 1 June.', 'F'], ['A delayed monsoon can affect water supply.', 'T'], ['This year\'s monsoon was delayed.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'The flight school uses single-engine aircraft for the first 120 hours of training and twin-engine aircraft for the remainder. Students fly solo only after their instructor certifies them as competent.', s: [['Students fly twin-engine aircraft in the first 50 hours.', 'F'], ['Instructor certification is required before solo flight.', 'T'], ['The school has more single-engine than twin-engine aircraft.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'Automation reduces workload in normal operations, but research shows that pilots who rely heavily on it may lose manual flying skills. Some airlines now encourage manual flying in suitable conditions.', s: [['Automation increases workload in normal operations.', 'F'], ['Some airlines encourage manual flying.', 'T'], ['All airlines ban manual flying above 10,000 ft.', 'C']] },
    { p: 'Hydraulic systems on large aircraft are usually duplicated or triplicated so that the failure of one system does not cause loss of control. Each system has its own pumps and reservoirs.', s: [['Large aircraft usually have more than one hydraulic system.', 'T'], ['All hydraulic systems share one reservoir.', 'F'], ['Hydraulic failures are the most common technical fault.', 'C']] },
  ];

